\name{Option}
\alias{Option}
\title{An option contract, the right but not the obligation to buy the underlying at the strike price, for a call, or to sell it, for a put}
\description{
It holds the members every option shares: its moneyness against the underlying, its premium split into intrinsic and time value, and its implied volatility and greeks from \code{BlackScholes} or \code{Black76}. The family classes such as \code{EquityOption} inherit it, and each carries the discovery functions \code{expiries()}, \code{strikes()} and \code{chain()} on its class generator, reading its own segment. Built directly, \code{Option} accepts any option, including one on an index.

The pricing methods treat the option as European and without dividends, and take it to expire at 15:30 India time on its expiry date, which is what UBI's own order engine assumes. MCX commodity options trade until later in the evening, so for them 15:30 is an approximation.

The examples below show its properties and the functions on its class generator, in this order:
\itemize{
\item For \code{Option$expiries()}, list the next five Nifty option expiries.
\item For \code{Option$expiries()}, compare how many option expiries are listed on an index and on a share.
\item For \code{Option$strikes()}, print the lowest and highest strikes and how many there are for the nearest Reliance option expiry.
\item For \code{Option$strikes()}, find the at-the-money strike, the listed strike nearest the Nifty level.
\item For \code{Option$chain()}, print the first rows of the nearest Nifty option chain.
\item For \code{Option$chain()}, count the calls and the puts in a Reliance option chain.
\item For \code{Option$chain()}, build the three calls nearest the money from the chain's instrument ids and print their prices.
\item For \code{is_call}, check the kind of an at-the-money Nifty option.
\item For \code{is_call}, split a list of options into calls and puts.
\item For \code{is_put}, check that a contract built with the \code{PE} option type is a put.
\item For \code{is_put}, show that a call is not a put.
\item For \code{intrinsic_value}, print the intrinsic value of the at-the-money call and put.
\item For \code{intrinsic_value}, compare the intrinsic value of a deep in-the-money Reliance call with its premium.
\item For \code{time_value}, print how much of the at-the-money Nifty call's premium is time value.
\item For \code{time_value}, compare the time value of the call and the put at the same strike.
\item For \code{in_the_money}, say whether the at-the-money call and put are in the money right now.
\item For \code{in_the_money}, count the in-the-money calls among five strikes around the money.
\item For \code{moneyness_percent}, print how far the at-the-money call and put are from the money.
\item For \code{moneyness_percent}, print the moneyness of the lowest and highest Reliance call strikes, one deep in and one far out of the money.
\item For \code{breakeven_price}, print the level the Nifty must reach by expiry for a buyer of the at-the-money call to break even.
\item For \code{breakeven_price}, print the move needed to break even for the call and the put, as a percentage of the index.
\item For \code{premium_per_lot}, print what one lot of the at-the-money Nifty call costs.
\item For \code{premium_per_lot}, work out how many lots of the call and the put a budget of Rs 50,000 buys.
\item For \code{notional_value}, print the value of the index one lot of the at-the-money call controls.
\item For \code{notional_value}, compare the premium with the notional value, which is the leverage an option gives.
}
}
